    "generator": "mulberry32, state = parseInt(sha256hex(seed).slice(0,8),16) = 0x56899d83 (same generator as the harness's seededRandomInt)",
    "procedure": "One generator stream for the campaign. Records in ascending id order (2tyf, 3tsf, 49dk, 65n9, 688p, 6hcn, 9ams, an5x, bpg8, f899, pcwk, qczx, s7rg, scck, t7hq). For each record with n sources: idx=[0..n-1]; for i in 0..4: j=i+rand(n-i); swap idx[i],idx[j]; sample = idx[0..4] in draw order. rand(m)=floor(mulberry32()*m).",
    "script_source": "// Draws 5 references per record for support checking.\n// Generator: mulberry32 seeded with parseInt(sha256(seed).slice(0,8),16), as in the harness.\n// Records in ascending id order, one generator stream for the whole campaign.\n// Per record: partial Fisher-Yates over source indices 0..n-1, i = 0..4, j = i + rand(n - i), swap; take first 5.\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { readFileSync, readdirSync } from \"node:fs\";\nconst seed = \"1c429ef1185544d68b26e4bb435dac41\";\nconst dir = process.argv[2];\nlet state = Number.parseInt(createHash(\"sha256\").update(seed).digest(\"hex\").slice(0, 8), 16);\nconst rand = (max) => {\n  state = (state + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\n  let t = Math.imul(state ^ (state >>> 15), 1 | state);\n  t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n  return Math.floor((((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296) * max);\n};\nconst out = {};\nfor (const f of readdirSync(dir).filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".json\")).sort()) {\n  const rec = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`${dir}/${f}`, \"utf8\"));\n  const n = rec.sources.length;\n  const idx = [...Array(n).keys()];\n  for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(5, n); i++) {\n    const j = i + rand(n - i);\n    [idx[i], idx[j]] = [idx[j], idx[i]];\n  }\n  out[rec.id] = { n, drawOrder: idx.slice(0, 5) };\n}\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ seed, seedState: createHash(\"sha256\").update(seed).digest(\"hex\").slice(0, 8), samples: out }, null, 1));\n",
